{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>You shall let it rest.</b> From work." "<b>And you shall leave it.</b> From eating after the time of gathering. Another interpretation: תִּשְׁמְטֶנָּה — from complete work, such as plowing and sowing; וּנְטַשְׁתָּהּ — from pruning and from hoeing (Sukkah 44)." "<b>And what they leave, the beasts of the field shall eat.</b> To liken the food of the poor person to the food of the beast: just as the beast eats without tithing, so too the poor eat without tithing — from here they said: there is no tithe in the seventh year (Mekhilta)." "<b>So shall you do to your vineyard.</b> And the beginning of the verse speaks of a white field, as is stated above it: ״הֵימֶנּוּ תִּזְרַע אֶת אַרְצֶךָ״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:06.438124222Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}